From 29a1a9fda766c09fe784e7e1ba2a882ab323aab6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:40:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: preserve interactive WebTransport when bulk preference
 is disabled

Add the bulk preference knob without changing its default. Chain-only
service hints can bypass UDP in prefer mode while explicit WT URLs, only
policy, Avalanche hints and browser-like peers retain WT selection. A
bypass does not create a failed-UDP cache entry or fallback failure metric.

Classify the current relay owner's two additional names, sendinvshort and
invshort, on TX_ANNOUNCE. Retain existing Merklix/TX_BODY mappings and
CONTROL for unknown names. Compare the two exact message tables and test
their union without importing the whole relay runtime or private version
negotiation.

Native daemon/unit builds pass 39/171 actions. Eleven URL/cache/policy/class
cases pass 330 assertions; the raw-fallback case passes 18 assertions. Bulk
routing 3.33s and existing fallback 6.09s functionals pass. Preserve the
initial fixture failure: a false Avalanche hint selected WT but its missing
proof/service correctly failed the ordinary Avalanche-only version check.
The corrected fixture tests routing with full-relay connections, not proof
or quorum behavior. Linux CPU, full merged relay, sanitizers, Safari and
performance sweeps were not run. Both transport defaults remain OFF.

